<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
    <title>Privacy Policy | My Reading List</title>
    <meta name="description" content="How My Reading List handles account information, reading lists, browser storage, and optional Open Library connections." />
    <link rel="canonical" href="https://www.myreadinglist.online/privacy" />
    <link rel="icon" type="image/svg+xml" href="/favicon.svg" />
  </head>
  <body>
    <main>
      <a class="back-link" href="/">Back to My Reading List</a>
      <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p class="updated">Last updated: October 10, 2026</p>
      <p>
        My Reading List at <a href="https://www.myreadinglist.online">www.myreadinglist.online</a> is operated by Anas, the maintainer of the My Reading List project.
        This policy explains how information is handled when you browse books,
        save reading lists, sign in, or connect Open Library.
      </p>

      <h2>Information used by the website</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Guest libraries:</strong> Books, reading statuses, preferences,
          cached book information, and pending changes are saved in your browser.
          Guest use does not require a website account. Connecting Open Library
          can also enable cloud storage through your verified Open Library account.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Website accounts:</strong> Clerk handles authentication with email
          codes, passwords, or Google. Clerk securely stores and checks website
          account passwords; this website never receives or stores them. Clerk processes account information such as your email address
          and, for Google sign-in, basic profile information such as your name and
          profile picture. The website uses your verified Clerk user ID to associate
          your account with your cloud library. It does not receive your Google password.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Cloud libraries:</strong> Neon stores saved book metadata, reading
          statuses, sync revisions, deletion markers, and account identifiers.
          Linking an existing Open Library library stores the association between
          your Open Library username and your website account.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Technical information:</strong> Hosting and authentication providers
          may process IP addresses, browser and device information, request times,
          and diagnostic logs to deliver and secure the service. Application errors
          may also be logged for troubleshooting.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Why this information is used</h2>
      <p>
        Information is used to authenticate you, save and synchronize your library,
        recover pending offline changes, provide book search and recommendations,
        operate an optional Open Library connection, and diagnose service problems.
        Recommendations use subjects and languages from your reading lists to look
        up related books. Website cloud libraries are not published as a public
        profile by this application.
      </p>

      <h2>Cookies and browser storage</h2>
      <p>
        Authentication uses cookies managed by Clerk. An Open Library connection
        uses an HTTP-only session cookie, and legacy cloud access uses a separate
        HTTP-only session cookie. Local storage keeps reading lists, preferences,
        account-specific caches, backups made during account switches, and queued
        sync changes on your device.
      </p>
      <p>
        Signing out hides the active website account's library, but does not erase
        its browser cache or pending changes. Clearing this site's browser data
        removes local copies and can permanently lose unsynced guest books.
        It does not delete copies already stored in the cloud or on Open Library.
      </p>

      <h2>Service providers and external requests</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><a href="https://clerk.com/legal/privacy">Clerk</a> provides website authentication and account management.</li>
        <li><a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy">Google</a> provides optional Google sign-in and fonts loaded on the main library page.</li>
        <li><a href="https://neon.com/privacy-policy">Neon</a> provides the cloud database.</li>
        <li><a href="https://vercel.com/legal/privacy-policy">Vercel</a> hosts the website and handles requests.</li>
        <li><a href="https://archive.org/about/terms.php">Open Library and Internet Archive</a> provide book search, metadata, cover images, and optional shelf synchronization.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        Book searches and recommendation queries are sent through the website's
        server to Open Library, or Internet Archive when search fallback is used.
        Cover images and fonts can be loaded directly from external services, which
        receive the technical information needed to serve those requests.
        These providers process information under their own policies and may
        process it outside your country.
      </p>

      <h2>Optional Open Library connection</h2>
      <p>
        Open Library is separate from your website account. If you choose to connect,
        your Open Library email and password, or Internet Archive access and secret
        keys, pass through this website's server to Open Library for login. The
        application does not save those passwords or keys in browser storage or
        the cloud database; it retains the resulting session in an HTTP-only cookie.
      </p>
      <p>
        While connected, adding, moving, or removing supported books can update
        your Open Library shelves, and shelf changes can be imported here.
        Shelf visibility is governed by Open Library's settings and policies.
        Disconnecting stops this integration on the current browser but does not
        delete your Open Library account or its shelves.
      </p>

      <h2>Retention and your choices</h2>
      <p>
        Local data remains until it is removed by you, the browser, or application
        storage updates. Cloud libraries remain available for synchronization;
        removing a book leaves a deletion marker to prevent older devices from
        restoring it. Signing out or deleting an authentication account does not
        automatically erase the separate Neon library or other local copies.
        Service providers may retain logs and backups according to their policies.
      </p>
      <p>
        You can use the site without a website account, remove books from your
        lists, disconnect Open Library, sign out, and clear this site's browser
        storage. To get a copy of, correct, or delete the data saved to your
        website account, email <a href="mailto:anasbutthussain@gmail.com">anasbutthussain@gmail.com</a> from
        the email address you use for your account and tell us what you'd
        like to do. We need to confirm the account belongs to you before sharing
        or deleting private data. Never email your password, sign-in or verification
        codes, or any secret login details from your browser or Internet Archive
        account. We won't ask you to send these.
      </p>

      <h2>Contact and policy updates</h2>
      <p>
        For privacy questions, contact <a href="mailto:anasbutthussain@gmail.com">anasbutthussain@gmail.com</a>.
        This page will be updated when the service's data practices change, with
        the revision date shown above.
      </p>
    </main>
